Algorithm 1: scContam audit pipeline

Input: Benchmark B, reference subsample R, scFM θ, donor and cell-type metadata.
Output: Per-cell $\{J^*(c), p_c\}$; donor-matched gap statistics and permutation p.

1 Step 1 (Signal A): Compute MinHash sketch ($m = 128$) for each $c \in \mathcal{B} \cup \mathcal{R}$;
2 for $c \in \mathcal{B}$ do
3 | Compute $J^*(c)$ via banded LSH ($b = 16$, $r = 8$) on $\mathcal{R}$;
4 | Draw 1000 permutation sketches; compute $p_c$ from Eq. 4;
5 end
6 Step 2 (Embedding): Extract $\theta$-embedding $e_c$ for all $c \in \mathcal{B}$;
7 Step 3 (Donor-matched gap):
8 for each $(t, d)$ pair with $n_{\text{clean}}, n_{\text{contam}} \geq n_{\text{min}}$ do
9 | Compute $\Delta_{(t, d), \theta}$ via Eq. 8;
10 end
11 Step 4 (Permutation null): Shuffle contamination labels within each $(t, d)$ group, repeat Step 3, $B = 500$ trials;
12 Step 5 (Negative control, optional): Repeat Steps 3–4 on a Signal-A-clean dataset with random pseudo-contamination;
